--TEST--
`new` naming an enum and a constructor reference to an enum are each one `E0870`, whose help says a case is written `M::Case`
--FILE--
<?nvs
enum Mode {
    Read,
    Write,
}

new Mode();
Mode $m = new Mode();
var $f = Mode::constructor;

echo Mode::Read as int, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0870]: `Mode` is an enum, so it has no constructor
%A
error[E0870]: `Mode` is an enum, so it has no constructor
%A
error[E0870]: `Mode` is an enum, so it has no constructor
